       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day, which is double the maximum labeled metformin dose. The usual maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. A single dose of 1700 mg is also well above the usual maximum of 850\u20131000 mg per dose. This dose raises the risk of severe lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum for immediate-release)\n- **1000 mg PO twice daily with meals** (2,000 mg/day)\n- **1700 mg total daily**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals\n\nIf 1700 mg three times daily is what you intend, tell me and I'll enter it with a note that you confirmed the above-maximum dose. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
